    <string name="legendary_riddle_title">Legendary riddle</string>
    <string name="legendary_riddle_intro">A gem from the catalog is hiding behind these clues. Find it, then point out its country of origin on the map.</string>
    <string name="legendary_clue_label">Clue %1$d</string>
    <string name="legendary_clue_1">In 1951, a British gemologist uncovered an unknown mineral — unaware he had just discovered what would remain, for nearly fifty years, the rarest gem mineral on Earth.</string>
    <string name="legendary_clue_2">Only one deposit in the world has ever produced it. Cut stones rarely exceed two carats.</string>
    <string name="legendary_clue_3">Its color ranges from brownish-red to orange, and its hardness rivals corundum — enough to fool more than one collector.</string>
    <string name="legendary_clue_4">Find on the map the country that holds this unique deposit, and prove you\'ve cracked the secret.</string>
